## Full feature list
You can see the full feature list [here](https://docs.khoj.dev/category/features).

## Self-Host

To get started with self-hosting Khoj, [read the docs](https://docs.khoj.dev/get-started/setup).

## Enterprise

Khoj is available as a cloud service, on-premises, or as a hybrid solution. To learn more about Khoj Enterprise, [visit our website](https://khoj.dev/teams).

## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)

Q: Can I use Khoj without self-hosting?

Yes! You can use Khoj right away at [https://app.khoj.dev](https://app.khoj.dev) — no setup required.

Q: What kinds of documents can Khoj read?

Khoj supports a wide variety: PDFs, Markdown, Notion, Word docs, org-mode files, and more.

Q: How does Khoj avoid duplicate Jira tickets?

Use `find_similar_jira_ticket()` to check existing issues before creating a new one:

```python
ticket = await find_similar_jira_ticket(
    ""Dashboard panes break layout when zoomed"", user
)
if ticket:
    print(f""A similar ticket already exists: {ticket}"")
```

Q: Will Khoj mention existing Jira tickets when I chat with it?

Yes. When you describe a problem, Khoj searches the synced Jira tickets and
adds any matching issue text to the conversation context. If a ticket is found
you'll see a status message with the ticket key and the bot's reply will include
its details.

Q: How can I make my own agent?

Check out [this blog post](https://blog.khoj.dev/posts/create-agents-on-khoj/) for a step-by-step guide to custom agents.
For more questions, head over to our [Discord](https://discord.gg/BDgyabRM6e)!


