agent.py,backend/myenv/Lib/site-packages/langchain/agents/agent.py,6d1facd3e52ca4d5f7650f9bc943f269396af516,samstuewart/Gem-Bot,https://api.github.com/repositories/1005727717/contents/backend/myenv/Lib/site-packages/langchain/agents/agent.py?ref=6633cf1d11b70837696fd459ecf83e0776e9b7c6,https://api.github.com/repositories/1005727717/git/blobs/6d1facd3e52ca4d5f7650f9bc943f269396af516,https://github.com/samstuewart/Gem-Bot/blob/6633cf1d11b70837696fd459ecf83e0776e9b7c6/backend/myenv/Lib/site-packages/langchain/agents/agent.py,"A lightweight Flask-based chatbot backend powered by LangChain and Ollama LLM, designed to provide natural and helpful responses to user queries. It leverages Gemma:2B via Ollama, with a structured prompt pipeline and seamless CORS-enabled API for frontend integration.",,0,0,0,5,2025-06-20T18:03:09Z,0,0,"# Gem Bot – A Lightweight LLM Chatbot Backend
Gem Bot is a simple and modular Flask-based chatbot backend that leverages Ollama’s Gemma:2B language model and LangChain to deliver natural and helpful responses. It exposes a REST API, making it easy to integrate with any frontend interface.

## Features

Powered by Ollama + Gemma 2B local LLM

LangChain integration with structured prompt and output parsing

CORS-enabled Flask backend for cross-origin access

API-ready for chat-based frontend integration

Environment-based secure configuration

## Getting Started

Clone the repository and navigate to the project folder.

Set up a Python virtual environment.

Install dependencies using pip install -r requirements.txt.

Create a .env file and add the following keys:

OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_key

LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=your_langchain_key

LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=GemBot

LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true

Run the server using python app.py.

Your backend will be live at: http://localhost:5000

## API Endpoints

GET /
Returns: { ""message"": ""Chatbot backend is running!"" }

POST /chat
Payload: { ""message"": ""Your question here"" }
Returns: { ""response"": ""Chatbot's reply"" }

## License
MIT License — Free to use and modify for personal or commercial projects.

