azuresearch.py,.venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain_community/vectorstores/azuresearch.py,7d2142a1fb02b24e88e7bb7bbbafe05908c79d22,priyankt3i/UnstructuredDirectoryLoader,https://api.github.com/repositories/839431332/contents/.venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain_community/vectorstores/azuresearch.py?ref=e1cfaa7097bfe02de5a39420960d4d823a804f42,https://api.github.com/repositories/839431332/git/blobs/7d2142a1fb02b24e88e7bb7bbbafe05908c79d22,https://github.com/priyankt3i/UnstructuredDirectoryLoader/blob/e1cfaa7097bfe02de5a39420960d4d823a804f42/.venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain_community/vectorstores/azuresearch.py,"UnstructuredDirectoryLoader uses 🦜️🔗 LangChain <langchain_community.document_loaders.unstructured> UnstructuredFileLoader to load files like '.txt', '.csv', '.pdf', '.msg' into a List[Document] using 🦜️🔗 LangChain <langchain_core.documents> Document",,0,0,0,11,2024-08-07T17:01:22Z,1,0,"# What is UnstructuredDirectoryLoader?

- UnstructuredDirectoryLoader uses 🦜️🔗 LangChain <langchain_community.document_loaders.unstructured> **UnstructuredFileLoader** to load files like '.txt', '.csv', '.pdf', '.msg' into a List[Document] using  🦜️🔗 LangChain <langchain_core.documents> **Document**

## How to install

The Python version used when this was developed was 3.9 :open_mouth:

```
pip install UnstructuredDirectoryLoader
```

### How to use

1. Just pass you local directory path in UnstructuredDirectoryLoader() and then use this directory loader.

    ```
    directory_loader = UnstructuredDirectoryLoader(directory_path='*<Your_Local_Folder_Path>*')
    ```

    ```
    listDocs = directory_loader.load()
    ```

3. Done! Go ahead and use a text splitter on this docs

    ```
    text_splitter = SemanticChunker(HuggingFaceEmbeddings())
    ```
